From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: FullPanel arms a full screen entered without the notch

What: in "Full screen including notch" (FullPanel), the main window's full
screen on a display without a camera housing is armed late instead of
being normal full screen for good. It is normal full screen there, as a
full screen a display change moved there (released, a display change with
its own 3 tries), and says so once with a line omacvm check does not warn
about ("in full screen on a display without a camera housing (the
MacBook's display is off): ..."; beside the open MacBook the old "a window
on another display ..." line). didEnterFullScreen counts it as entered
(the retake and the sorting of later frame changes need that). Once
AppKit has its Space on a display with a housing (the lid opened, the
external display unplugged), the existing paths take the strip: the claim
(AppKit lays it out under the reservation answer: "strip covered"), else
the retake once the displays settle ("strip taken again", then "strip
covered"). On the way back to a display with a housing (any full screen)
a "display change: ..." line comes first, which omacvm check warns about
until "strip covered". A full screen armed late takes the strip only on a
display of the size this start's notch was measured on
(OMACVM_FULLPANEL_PANEL from OmacVM.app): on another size it stays normal
full screen with a line ("... start the VM again for the strip"), as the
guest's bar was given that notch for the whole boot. The other displays'
windows (made again per display) stay as before; so does an entry where
another part is missing (the menu bar always shown, no reservation, no
SkyLight), whose line now names that part.

Why: #716 (reported by @hadiskeini). A VM started in "Full screen including
notch" with the lid closed (an external display only) kept a black strip
beside the notch after the lid was opened and the external display
unplugged, until the VM was started again (the guest 3456x2160 instead of
3456x2234 on a 16-inch MacBook Pro). OmacVM.app now gives such a start
FullPanel with the notch it measured last on this Mac; but QEMU armed a
full screen only when it was entered on a display with a housing
(-willEnterFullScreen returned before armed), and the claim, the resume
after a display without a housing and the retake all need an armed full
screen, so its Space never took the strip on the MacBook's display.

Fallbacks: anything this needs that is missing gives today's behaviour:
normal full screen below the notch, with the retake's lines ("strip not
back ..."); leaving and entering full screen on the MacBook's display
still covers the strip. A Split View tile is never taken.

Upstream: not applicable (private AppKit, OmacVM's notch strip).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-fullpanel-late-arm.sh (the rules,
and the wiring in the patched ui/cocoa.m at build time; --self-test: the
wiring checks fail on the code before), test-fullpanel-retake.c (a late
entry replayed: arrival at full height, AppKit keeping the band, Split
View and a later display change after it, quiet on the external display,
another panel size); the strip itself only on a notched Mac
(src/tests/e2e/display-unplug.sh, case fullpanel-clamshell). Applies
after omacvm-cocoa-fullpanel-retake.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -3559,6 +3559,8 @@
     int retake_reasks;         /* asked again after a wait since the last trigger */
     bool retake_tried;         /* a try in this full screen: retake_settle is its settle */
     unsigned retake_settle;    /* omacvm_fullpanel_settles at the last try */
+    /* Armed late (omacvm-cocoa-fullpanel-late-arm.patch). */
+    bool late;                 /* entered on a display without a housing, no strip yet */
 }
 - (id)initWithWindow:(NSWindow *)w;
 - (bool)claimsStrip;
@@ -3572,6 +3574,7 @@
 - (bool)retakeTaken;
 - (void)retakeExpired;
 - (void)retakeGiveUp:(const char *)reason;
+- (bool)lateFits;
 @end
 
 /*
@@ -3585,6 +3588,19 @@
 /* Settles of the displays so far (the display update ran): one try per settle. */
 static unsigned omacvm_fullpanel_settles;
 
+/*
+ * FullPanel armed late (#716): its rules, included here and not with the
+ * other headers above, so the later patches' context there stays as it is.
+ */
+#include "ui/omacvm-fullpanel-late.h"
+/*
+ * The panel this start's notch was measured on (OMACVM_FULLPANEL_PANEL,
+ * omacvm-cocoa-fullpanel-late-arm.patch): a full screen armed late takes
+ * the strip only on a display of that size.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_fullpanel_panel_given;
+static double omacvm_fullpanel_panel_w, omacvm_fullpanel_panel_h;
+
 static char omacvm_fullpanel_state_key;
 static char omacvm_fullpanel_titlebar_context;
 static char omacvm_fullpanel_options_context;
@@ -4036,10 +4052,22 @@
 - (bool)claimsStrip
 {
     return window && omacvm_fp_claims(inside, armed, rejected, lost, omacvm_fullpanel_menu_failed,
-                                      omacvm_fullpanel_notch(window));
+                                      omacvm_fullpanel_notch(window)) && [self lateFits];
 }
 
 /*
+ * A full screen armed late is on a display of the panel this start's
+ * notch was measured on (omacvm_fp_late_fits); any other full screen fits.
+ */
+- (bool)lateFits
+{
+    NSRect f = [[window screen] frame];
+
+    return omacvm_fp_late_fits(late, omacvm_fullpanel_panel_given, omacvm_fullpanel_panel_w,
+                               omacvm_fullpanel_panel_h, f.size.width, f.size.height);
+}
+
+/*
  * Before AppKit lays the window out for full screen (every way in posts
  * it first, before the reservation question): this full screen's parts.
  */
@@ -4048,18 +4076,33 @@
     NSScreen *screen = [window screen];
     double notch = screen ? [screen safeAreaInsets].top : 0;
     bool always = [[NSUserDefaults standardUserDefaults] boolForKey:@"AppleMenuBarVisibleInFullscreen"];
-    OmacVMFPFallback fallback;
+    bool in_the_way = omacvm_fp_menu_bar_in_the_way(always, immersive_mode_enabled);
+    bool main_window = ![window isKindOfClass:objc_getClass("OmacVMHeadWindow")];
+    bool beside = omacvm_fullpanel_beside_builtin(window);
+    OmacVMFPFallback fallback, with_housing;
+    OmacVMFPEntry entry;
 
     [self releaseSystemState];
     [self endFullScreen];
     inside = true;
-    fallback = omacvm_fp_fallback(notch, omacvm_fp_menu_bar_in_the_way(always, immersive_mode_enabled),
-                                  notch > 0 && omacvm_fullpanel_install_reservation(),
+    fallback = omacvm_fp_fallback(notch, in_the_way, notch > 0 && omacvm_fullpanel_install_reservation(),
                                   omacvm_fullpanel_skylight() && !omacvm_fullpanel_menu_failed);
-    if (fallback != OMACVM_FP_OK) {
+    /*
+     * The main window on a display without a camera housing (the lid
+     * closed, or an external display beside the open MacBook): what a
+     * display with one would say, for the late arm (#716).
+     */
+    with_housing = fallback;
+    if (fallback == OMACVM_FP_NO_NOTCH && main_window) {
+        with_housing = omacvm_fp_fallback(1, in_the_way, omacvm_fullpanel_install_reservation(),
+                                          omacvm_fullpanel_skylight() && !omacvm_fullpanel_menu_failed);
+    }
+    entry = omacvm_fp_entry(fallback, with_housing, main_window);
+    if (entry == OMACVM_FP_ENTRY_NORMAL) {
+        fallback = omacvm_fp_entry_why(fallback, with_housing, main_window);
         if (!fallback_logged) {
             fallback_logged = true;
-            if (omacvm_fp_fallback_checked(fallback, omacvm_fullpanel_beside_builtin(window))) {
+            if (omacvm_fp_fallback_checked(fallback, beside)) {
                 fprintf(stderr, "omacvm: full panel: %s: normal full screen\n",
                         omacvm_fp_fallback_text(fallback));
             } else {
@@ -4070,12 +4113,30 @@
     }
     armed = true;
     reveal = !immersive_mode_enabled;
+    if (entry == OMACVM_FP_ENTRY_LATE) {
+        /*
+         * Armed late: normal full screen on this display, as one a display
+         * change moved here (released, a display change with its own
+         * tries); the resume and the retake take the strip once AppKit has
+         * its Space on a display with a housing. Not a line omacvm check
+         * warns about.
+         */
+        late = released = true;
+        [self retakeNewChange];
+        fallback_logged = true;
+        if (beside) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "omacvm: full panel: a window on another display than the built-in one: macOS's own full screen there\n");
+        } else {
+            fprintf(stderr, "omacvm: full panel: in full screen on a display without a camera housing (the MacBook's display is off): the strip is taken once the window is on the MacBook's display\n");
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 /* Everything of the last full screen forgotten (the logs may come again). */
 - (void)endFullScreen
 {
     inside = armed = entered = accepted = rejected = lost = released = reveal = false;
+    late = false;
     own_known = false;
     covered_logged = reveal_logged = fallback_logged = options_logged = false;
     displaced = display_changed = lost_tile = retake_pending = retake_asked = retake_given_up = false;
@@ -4102,6 +4163,8 @@
     if (verdict == OMACVM_FP_ACCEPTED) {
         accepted = true;
         accepted_display = [[window screen] frame];
+        /* A late one has the strip: an ordinary FullPanel full screen from here. */
+        late = false;
         return;
     }
     accepted = false;
@@ -4118,7 +4181,8 @@
 - (void)didEnterFullScreen:(NSNotification *)notification
 {
     [self verify:true];
-    if (!armed || !accepted) {
+    /* Armed late counts as entered too: the retake and the frame sorting need it. */
+    if (!omacvm_fp_entered(armed, accepted, late)) {
         return;
     }
     entered = true;
@@ -4625,10 +4689,20 @@
         [self releaseSystemState];
         fprintf(stderr, "omacvm: full panel: the full screen is on a display without a camera housing: normal full screen there\n");
         [self relayout];
+    } else if (late && !rejected && omacvm_fp_screen_resumes(released, full, omacvm_fullpanel_notch(window)) &&
+               ![self lateFits]) {
+        /* Armed late, on a display of another size than this start's notch was measured on. */
+        rejected = true;
+        released = displaced = false;
+        fprintf(stderr, "omacvm: full panel: the MacBook's display is %.0fx%.0f now, this start's notch was measured at %.0fx%.0f: normal full screen; start the VM again for the strip\n",
+                [screen frame].size.width, [screen frame].size.height,
+                omacvm_fullpanel_panel_w, omacvm_fullpanel_panel_h);
     } else if (omacvm_fp_screen_resumes(released, full, omacvm_fullpanel_notch(window))) {
         /* On a display with a housing again: the next displacement is a new display change. */
         released = displaced = false;
         covered_logged = false;
+        /* omacvm check warns about this until "strip covered" (also when AppKit gives it at once). */
+        fprintf(stderr, "omacvm: full panel: display change: the full screen is on a display with a camera housing again; the strip comes back once the displays settle\n");
         [self relayout];
         [self comeBack];
     } else if (full) {
@@ -5109,6 +5183,8 @@
         return;
     }
     fprintf(stderr, "omacvm: full panel: asked for (OMACVM_FULLPANEL=1)\n");
+    omacvm_fullpanel_panel_given = omacvm_fp_panel(getenv("OMACVM_FULLPANEL_PANEL"),
+                                                   &omacvm_fullpanel_panel_w, &omacvm_fullpanel_panel_h);
     (void)omacvm_fullpanel_install_reservation();
     (void)omacvm_fullpanel_skylight();
     [[NSNotificationCenter defaultCenter]
